= V1 public corpus inventory =

The V1 inventory is no longer maintained manually page-by-page in this document. The repository contains an exhaustive reproducible snapshot generated directly from the anonymous MediaWiki Action API.

== Current snapshot ==
* 186 public pages across 24 nonnegative namespaces
* 606 archived revision bodies
* 162 Main pages
* 9 Template pages
* 162 used category names / 0 created Category pages
* 4 Property pages
* 3 <code>smw/schema</code> pages
* 6 MediaWiki pages
* 2 File description pages
* 0 Concept pages
* 0 Module pages

== Canonical inventory surfaces ==
<pre>
archive-v1/audit.json                 completeness + counts
archive-v1/index.json                 every public page record
archive-v1/namespaces/*/index.json    exhaustive titles by namespace
archive-v1/pages/*                    exact current wikitext
archive-v1/history/*                  complete captured revision bodies
archive-v1/templates/index.json       all implemented templates
archive-v1/templates/usage/*          every transclusion caller
archive-v1/categories/index.json      all used/created categories
archive-v1/categories/members/*       complete memberships
archive-v1/special/*                  maintenance reports
</pre>

The archive follows MediaWiki continuation until no continuation token remains and is regenerated by <code>scripts/archive_v1.py</code> / the GitHub archive workflow.

== Interpretation ==
A source being archived does not by itself decide its V2 disposition. It establishes evidence before editorial action.

<pre>
archive
→ compare revisions / related objects
→ identify unique writing, semantics and behavior
→ distinguish design intent from deployed implementation
→ choose V2 role
→ publish / redirect / retire deliberately
</pre>

See [[BITwiki:V1 implementation audit]], [[BITwiki:V1 category migration]], [[BITwiki:Templates and categories]] and [[BITwiki:Editorial protocol]].

